nce in evidence-based practice?</article-title><source>J Adv Nurs</source><year>2004</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>81</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15186471</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1365-2648.2004.03068.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pope</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>van Royen</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Baker</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Qualitative methods in research on healthcare quality</article-title><source>Qual Saf Health Care</source><year>2002</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>148</fpage><lpage>152</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12448807</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/qhc.11.2.148</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wallace</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Hatzakis</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Legro</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldstein</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Understanding a VA preventive care clinical reminder : lessons learned</article-title><source>SCI Nurs</source><year>2004</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>149</fpage><lpage>152</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15553058</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>